==English==

===Alternative spellings===
* [[Mohammed]], [[Mohamed]], [[Mohamet]], [[Muhamed]]

===Etymology===
From Arabic {{Arab|[[محمد]]}} (''muħámmad'', [[praise]]d, [[commendable]], [[laudable]]), the past participle of {{Arab|[[حمد]]}} (''ħámida'', to [[praise]], [[commend]], [[laud]], [[extol]]).

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# The [[prophet]] who [[founded]] [[Islam]].
# A male given name, esp. in Islamic culture.

